# boundaries.denylist — the term deny-lists of `make verify-boundaries`
# (scripts/ci/verify_boundaries.sh; SC-017, FR-049, FR-085, FR-007). Reviewed
# like code: adding or removing a line changes what CI enforces.
#
# Format: <category><TAB or spaces><Python regex>. Matching is case-insensitive
# unless the regex scopes it off with (?-i:…). Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Categories:
#   migration        SC-017(a) / FR-049 — a proprietary vendor controller, network
#                    services orchestrator, network controller product, vendor
#                    fabric-automation product (incl. the NOS vendor's own, Nokia
#                    Event Driven Automation — platform-coupling.md PC-21),
#                    proprietary network element driver, or the retired system
#                    name. Scanned over every first-party text file.
#   retired-service  FR-085 — a retired service name (the migration aliases of
#                    contracts/construct-vocabulary.md). Scanned over documentation
#                    (*.md, and everything under docs/); a hit passes only in a
#                    labelled context: its own line, or the nearest heading above
#                    it, says alias / migration / provenance / historical / history
#                    / retired.
#   placement        SC-017(c) / FR-007 — a Compose or outside-Kubernetes
#                    deployment of platform applications. Scanned over every
#                    first-party non-Markdown text file (Compose files are also
#                    refused by file name).
#
# Allowed contexts (never scanned): the specification under specs/ (SC-017's own
# "Scope and interpretation", platform-coupling.md, research.md), this file, the
# checker itself, its fixture tests under tests/unit/verifyboundaries/, and trees
# that are not this repository's code — the upstream reference checkouts
# config-server/, data-server/, kuid/, sdcio-docs/, and node_modules/, .venv/,
# .specstride/, .specify/, .mixture-of-loops/, prompts/ (git-ignored scratch),
# bin/, .evidence/.

# --- (a) migration boundary: proprietary controllers, orchestrators, element drivers
migration   \bEvent[- ]Driven Automation\b
migration   \b(?-i:EDA)\b
migration   \bdocs\.eda\.dev\b
migration   \bFabric Services System\b
migration   \bNokia (?:NSP|Network Services Platform)\b
migration   \bNetwork Services Orchestrator\b
migration   \b(?-i:NSO)\b
migration   \bncs_cli\b
migration   \bnetwork element drivers?\b
migration   \bcisco-(?:ios|iosxr|nx|asa)-cli\b
migration   \bApstra\b
migration   \bCloudVision\b
migration   \bArista CVP\b
migration   \bCisco ACI\b
migration   \b(?-i:APIC)\b
migration   \bNexus Dashboard\b
migration   \b(?-i:DCNM)\b
migration   \bCrosswork\b
migration   \bJuniper (?:Paragon|Contrail)\b
# the retired system: the predecessor platform's own component names
migration   \bsonicprovider\b
migration   \bfabric-executor\b

# --- FR-085: retired service names (migration aliases), documentation only
retired-service   \bVPLS\b
retired-service   \bVPWS\b
retired-service   \bE-?Line\b
retired-service   \bL3VPN\b
retired-service   \bL2L3-?IRB\b

# --- (c) placement boundary: no Compose / outside-Kubernetes deployment
placement   \b(?:docker|podman)[- ]compose\b.*\b(?:up|run|start|create)\b
placement   \bcompose\s+up\b
